dialogue tavernkeeper
  node root marta "Clerk! Sit down. Everyone knows whose son you are. You've a face like an unfiled form."
    > "What's everyone celebrating?" -> marrow
    # One of these fills the second slot, depending on how far along we are.
    > "I need a favour." if not knows_key and not marta_paid -> favour
    > "Bramwick says you have his drawer key." if knows_key and not marta_paid -> key
    > "Thanks again for the key." if marta_paid -> thanks
    > "Bramwick still owes you a game of cards." if seen_iou and marta_paid -> iou
    > "Nothing. Goodnight." -> bye
  node marrow marta "The Marrow sails for the Straits at dawn. Half the room drinks to a safe voyage. The other half bets against it, and drinks faster."
    > "Ships keep vanishing out there." -> straits
    > "Who sails on her?" -> crew
    > "Goodnight, Marta." -> bye
  node crew marta "Vane, who could out-stare a gull. Hobb, the bosun, with more names on his arm than I have on my slate."
    -> crew2
  node crew2 marta "And the lookout can spot a lie at two miles. She misses every compliment. Mind her. She bites, and she's usually right."
    > "Ships keep vanishing out there." -> straits
    > "I'll mind her. Goodnight." -> bye
  node iou marta "Thirty years he's owed me that game. He'll never pay. Paying would mean it's over."
    -> iou2
  node iou2 marta "…Don't you dare tell him I said that. I'll water your punch."
    > "Your secret's safe. I'm a civil servant." -> bye
    > "He keeps it at the front of the drawer." -> front
  node front marta "Does he. …Get out of my tavern, clerk, before I start liking you."
  node straits marta "Six ships gone in three years. Five came back empty. Your father's never come back at all."
    -> straits2
  node straits2 marta "…You're signing on. Don't argue. I can see it. He had that look too."
    > "Goodnight, Marta." -> bye
  node favour marta "A favour is a debt with better manners. I take rum, gossip and truth, in that order. Come back with one."
    > "Rum, gossip, truth. In that order. Noted." -> bye
  node key marta "Won it off him at cards. He bet a pair of threes, the old fool. Yours for a bottle of rum. Mine's on the pier, held by customs."
    > "I've inspected some right here." if has rum -> traded
      take rum
      give drawer_key
      set marta_paid
      note marta_key "Marta won Bramwick's drawer key and would not give it back for nothing. One bottle of her own impounded rum, for the punch, is apparently the rate."
      sound pickup
    > "One bottle. Done." if not has rum -> bye
    > "Held by customs? Which customs?" if not has rum -> norum
  node norum marta "You, clerk. A crate on the quay says HELD FOR CUSTOMS INSPECTION. Nobody has come to inspect it."
    -> norum2
  node norum2 marta "My punch bowl's dry. So inspect it. It's nailed shut, so bring a crowbar. If a bottle comes loose, that's procedure."
    > "A crowbar. For procedure. Noted." -> bye
  node traded marta "You inspected it? With a crowbar? That's the best customs has done for me in thirty years."
    -> traded2
  node traded2 marta "Here's his key. Tell him a pair of threes is not a strategy."
    > "Goodnight, Marta." -> bye
  node thanks marta "Thanks are free, clerk, and I don't deal in free. Pay me in story. Come back and tell me what's in the Straits. I hate an unfinished story."
    > "I will. I'll even get it stamped." -> bye
  node bye marta "Go on. And shut the door. The gossip gets out."
